 F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {x}^{2}z & 0 & {x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(0)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(0)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}z)]k \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-0)i-(2xy-{x}^{2})j+(0-0)k \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\,i+({x}^{2}-2xy)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+2G) & =∇\\times F+2∇\\times G \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\,i+({x}^{2}-2xy)\\,j+2[{x}^{2}z\\,i+(xy-2xyz)\\,j-xz\\,k] \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}z)\\,i+({x}^{2}-2xy+2xy-4xyz)\\,j-2xz\\,k \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(1+2z)\\,i+({x}^{2}-4xyz)\\,j-2xz\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(1,1,1),$ we get\n\n$$\n(∇\\times (F+2G))(1,1,1)=3\\,i-3\\,j-2\\,k.\n$$" 13194139536104 17592186045417 true] [17592186181075 1075 #edb/ref 17592186181076 13194139536104 17592186045417 false] [17592186181075 1075 #edb/ref 17592186181077 13194139536104 17592186045417 false] [17592186181075 1075 #edb/ref 17592186181078 13194139536104 17592186045417 false] [17592186181075 1075 #edb/ref 17592186181079 13194139536104 17592186045417 false] [17592186181075 1075 #edb/ref 17592186181080 13194139536104 17592186045417 false] [17592186181075 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565688 13194139536104 17592186045417 true] [17592186181075 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565700 13194139536104 17592186045417 true] [17592186181075 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565842 13194139536104 17592186045417 true] [17592186181075 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565914 13194139536104 17592186045417 true] [17592186181075 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566095 13194139536104 17592186045417 true] [17592186181075 1078 #edb/ref 17592186565700 13194139536104 17592186045417 true] [17592186181087 1075 #edb/ref 17592186181088 13194139536104 17592186045417 false] [17592186181087 1075 #edb/ref 17592186181089 13194139536104 17592186045417 false] [17592186181087 1075 #edb/ref 175